 ## Overview
-A neural network module that predicts a depth distribution for each ray from image features by discretizing the depth range into buckets, predicting a probability density function (PDF) and intra-bucket offsets, and sampling from this distribution to determine depth values [S1, unofficial]. It differs from the sibling [DepthPredictor](4097-depthpredictor.md) by explicitly modeling depth uncertainty via a discrete probability distribution over sampled buckets rather than predicting a single deterministic depth value [S1, unofficial]. It is wrapped in a PyTorch Autograd Function to enable gradient flow, building on [Differentiable Depth Function Forward/Backward Pass](1047-differentiable-depth-function-forward-backward-pass.md) [G].
+A neural network module that predicts a depth distribution for each ray from image features by discretizing the depth range into buckets, predicting a probability density function (PDF) and intra-bucket offsets, and sampling from this distribution to determine depth values [S1, unofficial]. It differs from standard cost volume aggregation by explicitly modeling the uncertainty of depth hypotheses via a learnable projection and sampling mechanism, allowing for differentiable depth extraction and direct integration into ray marching pipelines [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-**Inputs:**
-- `features`: Tensor of shape `(batch, view, ray, surface, depth, 2)` containing projected features, where the last dimension holds raw PDF logits and raw offset logits [S1, unofficial].
-- `near`: Tensor of shape `(batch, view)` specifying the near plane distance [S1, unofficial].
-- `far`: Tensor of shape `(batch, view)` specifying the far plane distance [S1, unofficial].
-- `deterministic`: Boolean flag controlling whether sampling is deterministic (argmax) or stochastic [S1, unofficial].
-- `gaussians_per_pixel`: Integer specifying the number of samples (buckets) to draw from the depth distribution [S1, unofficial].
-- `use_transmittance`: Boolean flag determining whether opacity is computed via the transmittance formula or taken directly from the PDF density [S1, unofficial].
-
-**Outputs:**
-- `depth`: Tensor of shape `(batch, view, ray, surface, sample)` containing the predicted absolute depth values [S1, unofficial].
-- `opacity`: Tensor of shape `(batch, view, ray, surface, sample)` containing the predicted opacity values [S1, unofficial].
-- `pdf`: Tensor of shape `(batch, view, ray, surface, sample)` containing the sampled PDF values [S1, unofficial].
